The current screenshot’s marker is INTERVIEW-1-4d5f71db08bd59e6. Binary-search the shorter array for a partition where every left-side value is at most every right-side value. Time is O(log(min(m,n)+1)), within O(log(m+n)); auxiliary space is O(1).

```javascript
function solve(nums1, nums2) {
  let a = nums1;
  let b = nums2;
  if (a.length > b.length) [a, b] = [b, a];

  const m = a.length;
  const n = b.length;
  const half = Math.floor((m + n + 1) / 2);
  let low = 0;
  let high = m;

  while (low <= high) {
    const i = low + Math.floor((high - low) / 2);
    const j = half - i;

    const leftA = i === 0 ? -Infinity : a[i - 1];
    const rightA = i === m ? Infinity : a[i];
    const leftB = j === 0 ? -Infinity : b[j - 1];
    const rightB = j === n ? Infinity : b[j];

    if (leftA <= rightB && leftB <= rightA) {
      const leftMax = Math.max(leftA, leftB);
      if ((m + n) % 2 === 1) return leftMax;
      return (leftMax + Math.min(rightA, rightB)) / 2;
    }

    if (leftA > rightB) high = i - 1;
    else low = i + 1;
  }
}
```

Call solve(nums1, nums2) with ascending numeric arrays whose combined length is positive. It handles either array being empty, duplicates, and odd or even totals, without modifying the inputs; no imports, exports, or stdin/stdout are needed.

