Use two pointers, processing the side with the smaller running maximum. Time: O(n); extra space: O(1). Call solve(height) directly; no stdin/stdout, imports, or exports are needed.

```javascript
function solve(height) {
  let left = 0;
  let right = height.length - 1;
  let leftMax = 0;
  let rightMax = 0;
  let water = 0;

  while (left <= right) {
    if (leftMax <= rightMax) {
      leftMax = Math.max(leftMax, height[left]);
      water += leftMax - height[left];
      left++;
    } else {
      rightMax = Math.max(rightMax, height[right]);
      water += rightMax - height[right];
      right--;
    }
  }

  return water;
}
```

Empty arrays and arrays with fewer than three bars return 0; the displayed example returns 6.

